meta {
  name: 25 TAT Summary
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/tat/summary
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
  ~branchId: {{branchId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  TAT analytics (Turnaround Time.pdf §9) over the reports whose **current status
  is Approved**, read from the frozen `LabReport.tat*` snapshot columns (fast — no
  per-row recompute). A report that was Published or marked Error Reported is no
  longer Approved and is not counted, so `total` equals the Approved tab of the
  worklist (`GET /lab-reports/counts` -> `approved`) for the same filters.

  Query (all optional): the same filters as `GET /lab-reports/counts` — `branchId`
  (own branch by default, a branch id or `all`), `dateFrom`/`dateTo` (the ORDER's
  date, whole days, both ends inclusive), `departmentId`, `branchLabTestId`,
  `branchLabPanelId`, `referredByDoctorId`, `referralPanelId`, `sampleStatus`,
  `search`, `urgent`, `homeCollection`, ... `status` is ignored (always Approved).
  The caller's department/permission scope applies, as on the worklist.

  Response:
  `{ total, byBand: { WITHIN, WARNING, CRITICAL, BREACHED, UNKNOWN },
     avgNetMinutes, breachRate }`

  - `UNKNOWN` = approved but not computable at approval (no active schedule /
    no Max TAT configured).
  - `avgNetMinutes` = mean net working minutes across the counted reports (null if
    none).
  - `breachRate` = BREACHED / computable (0..1), null when no computable reports.
}
